   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the lease of lands located at the State University of New York at Albany",
    "basePrintNo": "S8221",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8221-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "New York State University",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S8221\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nauthorizing the lease of lands located at\nthe State University of New York at\nAlbany\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThis legislation would permit the construction of needed office\nand laboratory space that is required to support the University's\nlegislatively mandated mission of research.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nAuthorizes the State University of New York Trustees the power\nto lease and otherwise contract to make available 11.07 acres to\nFuller Road Management Corporation (FRMC) grounds and facilities\nof the campus of the University at Albany for the purpose of\nconstructing additional facilities to fulfill its legislatively\nmandated mission of research.\n\nAuthorizes the development, construction and operation of a\nbasic research, technology outreach business development and\noffice building, including additional office and laboratory space.\n\nSuch lease shall be a period not exceeding 40 years without any\nfee simple conveyance and otherwise upon terms and conditions\ndetermined by the Trustees, and subject to the approval of the\ndirector of the division of the budget, the attorney general and the\nstate comptroller.\n\nRequires Fuller Road Management Corporation to comply with the\nrequirements of article 15-A of the Executive Law and the\nrequirements of Article 8 sections 220, 240 and 241 of the Labor\nLaw.\n\nRequires that all work performed on such property ordinarily\nperformed by employees subject to Article 14 of the Civil\nService Law continue to be performed by such employees.\n\nRequires FRMC to comply with project labor agreement as defined\nin subdivision 1 or section 222 of the Labor Law for any single\nconstruction project exceeding $10 million in aggregate for which\nmore than 25 percent of such aggregate amount is furnished by\nState appropriations.\n\nAuthorizes FRMC to lease, sublease, construct, reconstruct,\nrehabilitate, improve, operate and manage the grounds and\nfacilities and to obtain funding or financing for the purposes\nof completing the project.\n\nRequires that any contracts entered into by FRMC and parties\ncontracting with FRMC be awarded by a competitive process.\n\nProvides that upon the expiration or termination of the lease, or in\nthe event that the property that is the subject of such lease is no\nlonger used for the purposes set forth in the legislation, the\nproperty and any improvements will revert to the state University of\nNew York.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis legislation would permit the\nconstruction of\nneeded office and laboratory space that is required to support the\nUniversity's legislatively mandated mission of research.\nSpecifically, the additional office and laboratory space will support\nthe University's College of Nanoscale Science and Engineering, the\nNew York State Center for Excellence in Nanoelectronics and\nassociated semiconductor research activities funded by active\npartnerships between government and private industry.\nFurthermore,such activity will promote economic development across\nthe capital region of New York State.\n\nThe legislature finds that granting the Trustees of the State University\nof New York the authority and power to lease and otherwise contract to\nmake available grounds and facilities of the campus of the University\nat Albany will promote the effective use of such lands for the\npublic good.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nL. 1990, Ch. 132; L. 1993, Ch. 40; L. 1997,\nCh. 643; L.2005, Ch. 541;\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
