    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S8221A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nauthorizing the lease of lands located at\nthe State University of New York at\nAlbany\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThis legislation would permit the\nconstruction of needed office and laboratory space that is required\nto support the University's legislatively mandated mission of research.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nAuthorizes the State University of New\nYork Trustees the power to lease and otherwise contract to make\navailable 11.07 acres to Fuller Road Management Corporation (FRMC)\ngrounds and facilities of the campus of the University at Albany for\nthe purpose of constructing additional facilities to fulfill its\nlegislatively mandated mission of research.\n\nAuthorizes the development, construction and operation of a basic\nresearch, technology outreach business development and office\nbuilding, including additional office and laboratory space.\n\nSuch lease shall be a period not exceeding 40 years without any fee\nsimple conveyance and otherwise upon terms and conditions determined\nby the Trustees, and subject to the approval of the director of the\ndivision of the budget, the attorney general and the state comptroller.\n\nRequires that all work performed on such property ordinarily performed\nby employees subject to Article 14 of the Civil Service Law continue\nto be performed by such employees.\n\nAuthorizes FRMC to lease, sublease, construct, reconstruct,\nrehabilitate, improve, operate and manage the grounds and facilities\nand to obtain funding or financing for the purposes of completing the\nproject.\n\nRequires that any contracts entered into by FRMC and parties\ncontracting with FRMC be awarded by a competitive process.\n\nProvides that upon the expiration or termination of the lease, or in\nthe event that the property that is the subject of such lease is no\nlonger used for the purposes set forth in the legislation, the\nproperty and any improvements will revert to the State University of\nNew York.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis legislation would permit the construction of\nneeded office and laboratory space that is required to support the\nUniversity's legislatively mandated mission of research.\nSpecifically, the additional office and laboratory space will support\nthe University's College of Nanoscale Science and Engineering, the\nNew York State Center for Excellence in Nanoelectronics and\nassociated semiconductor research activities funded by active\n\n\npartnerships between government and private industry.\nFurthermore, such activity will promote economic development across\nthe capital region of New York State.\n\nThe legislature finds that granting the Trustees of the State\nUniversity of New York the authority and power to lease and otherwise\ncontract to make available grounds and facilities of the campus of\nthe University at Albany will promote the effective use of such lands\nfor the public good.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nL. 1990, Ch. 132; L. 1993, Ch. 40; L. 1997,\nCh. 643; L.2005, Ch. 541;\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
